  "starterCode": "# SwiGLU FFN — reconstructed educational contract\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solution(x, w_gate, w_up, w_down):\n    # TODO: implement the operation described in the problem statement\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **SwiGLU FFN** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef solution(x, w_gate, w_up, w_down):\n    x=np.asarray(x,dtype=float); wg=np.asarray(w_gate,dtype=float); wu=np.asarray(w_up,dtype=float); wd=np.asarray(w_down,dtype=float)\n    gate=x@wg; up=x@wu\n    return ((gate/(1+np.exp(-gate)))*up @ wd).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
